Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: music_midi test fixtures
Comment: Test fixtures for the conductor (MIDI parsing, the tempo map, sequencing,
 the synthesizer seam and sample instruments). A composition and a given MIDI file
 carry separate rights, so each MIDI file below is from a Mutopia Project piece whose
 own page says "Copyright: Public Domain" - that per-piece line is authoritative, and
 it is quoted for each file with the page it was read from on 2026-10-20. The files
 are the downloads' verbatim bytes; the sha256 of each is recorded so a later
 download can be compared. Nothing here ships in a game.

Files: bach-invention-02.mid
Copyright: Public Domain
Comment: Johann Sebastian Bach (1685-1750), Invention 2 in C minor, BWV 773.
 Source edition: Bach-Gesellschaft. Typeset for the Mutopia Project by Allen Garvin
 (LilyPond 2.11.49), Mutopia-2008/06/15-58.
 Piece page: https://www.mutopiaproject.org/cgibin/piece-info.cgi?id=58
 Its line: "Copyright: Public Domain"
 Download: https://www.mutopiaproject.org/ftp/BachJS/BWV773/bach-invention-02/bach-invention-02.mid
 sha256: b61e1e4d4a42ca70efd0eb8a65de3ed0ca0ee9c31556354608f6caa360e78e98
License: public-domain

Files: dansenapolitaine.mid
Copyright: Public Domain
Comment: Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky (1840-1893), Napolitan Dance from Swan Lake,
 Op. 20 (1876), arranged for trumpet, percussion and piano by Laurence Sardain (a new
 arrangement, placed in the public domain on its page). Mutopia-2006/12/22-896,
 LilyPond 2.10.4.
 Piece page: https://www.mutopiaproject.org/cgibin/piece-info.cgi?id=896
 Its line: "Copyright: Public Domain"
 Download: https://www.mutopiaproject.org/ftp/TchaikovskyPI/dansenapolitaine/dansenapolitaine.mid
 sha256: 084540482e5522035447a44be092d38084c3308cdd2ea4f8c468b861f9fba43b
License: public-domain

Files: dansenapolitaine-type0.mid
Copyright: Public Domain
Comment: Derived from dansenapolitaine.mid above by scripts/make_type0_fixture.py
 (2026-10-20): the five tracks merged into the single track of an SMF type 0 file, and
 the tambourine track - which LilyPond writes as middle C on a melodic channel - moved
 to General MIDI percussion channel 10 as key 54, Tambourine. Re-running the script on
 the source above reproduces these bytes.
 sha256: 78e8f5effca0d7ecb41369e8a7f14bfc5bb6be602e9c27f6b03f57f7d2dfad18
License: public-domain

Files: dansenapolitaine-cast.mid
Copyright: Public Domain
Comment: Derived from dansenapolitaine-type0.mid above by scripts/make_cast_fixture.py
 (2026-10-20): a program change at tick 0 on each melodic channel, after the track
 name - the flute's channel 2 to program 73 (Flute), the two piano channels 4 and 5 to
 program 0 (Acoustic Grand Piano) - and nothing else; the tambourine stays on General
 MIDI percussion channel 10. LilyPond sets no program, so without them every part plays
 the piano. Re-running the script on the source above reproduces these bytes.
 sha256: cfe1333856e0576339662b2efbf799f3309a449a53227f31dbd3e3a05f908c6d
License: public-domain

